# Orbyza Agency - Cursor Intelligence Protocol

## Core Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router + Turbopack)
- **Backend**: Supabase (via @supabase/supabase-js)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 + Framer Motion
- **Architecture**: 6-Tool Stack (Antigravity -> GitHub -> v0 -> Cursor -> Supabase -> Vercel)

## Design System: "Cinematic Dark Mode"
- **Color Palette**: 
  - Primary: `#0EA5E9` (Sky Blue / High-tech Glow)
  - Secondary: `#F8FAFC` (Clean background for light areas)
  - Dark: `#0C4A6E` (Deep navy for high-contrast sections)
- **Aesthetic**:
  - Use `glass-card` class for container elements.
  - Apply `heading-xl` with uppercase black tracking-tighter for impact.
  - Use `framer-motion` for all transitions (scale, rotate, fade-in).
  - Backgrounds should use blur orbs (`blur-[150px]`) for depth.

## SEO Mandatory Rules
- Every page component MUST export a `Metadata` object.
- Include `alternates: { canonical: ... }` for all pages.
- Ensure only one `<h1>` per page.
- Use `JSON-LD` for services and blog posts (already integrated in ServiceDetail.tsx).

## Backend (Supabase) Rules
- Always use `import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabase'` for data fetching.
- For server-side privileged operations, use `getSupabaseAdmin()`.
- Reference the schema in `C:\Users\Ashok Sharma\.gemini\antigravity\brain\2aa57413-b5de-4f83-8c32-5c9ab3d963a6\supabase_schema.sql` for table structures.

## Deployment
- Deployment is automated via Vercel on push to `main`.
- Always verify local build (`npm run build`) before pushing complex UI changes.

## AI Instructions
- When refining UI, aim for "Absolute Dominance" aesthetic.
- Avoid generic placeholders; use cinematic copy (e.g., "Execution Vectors", "Intelligence Archive", "Surgical Marketing").
- Keep components small and focused.
